WEBVTT

NOTE WonderLang Beyond final trailer v10.

s001
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:03.970
Learn a language.

s002
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.360
Explore a world of mysteries.

s003
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.620
And rescue your brother…

s004
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.940
who’s still a beanie.

s005
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.740
Ben: I prefer “magically inconvenienced.”

s006
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.780
Hi, I’m Jonathan.
I’m the creator of WonderLang Beyond,

s007
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.600
a role-playing adventure
for intermediate language learners.

s008
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.960
Following the original WonderLang,
it brings even more fun ways

s008b
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.780
to practice your language skills
through gaming adventures.

s009
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.820
You’ll get to explore wild regions,
meet new characters, and solve mysteries,

s010
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.100
all while practicing your target language.

s011
00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.390 line:10%
Villager: If you’re looking for the traveler,
ask the shopkeeper. She spoke to him yesterday.

s012
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:43.230
Characters only speak your target language.
But don’t worry,

s013
00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.720
when a word is new,
you can just look it up.

s014
00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:49.850
You can also see how the sentence works
and bookmark it for later.

s015
00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.150
You’re part of the conversation, too.

s016
00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.450
You can build your reply word by word…

s017
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:01.110
[In Spanish]
I want to buy a potion for the journey.

s018
00:01:01.433 --> 00:01:02.700
Say it out loud.

s019
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.000
[In Japanese]
Where is the red forest?

s020
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.840
[Character, in Japanese]
Where is the red forest?

s021
00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.800
Or type your reply,
with a visual keyboard to help you along.

s022
00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:22.553 line:10%
Otter: Danger lurks in this forest.
Be careful.

s023
00:01:21.110 --> 00:01:26.270
Discover a new word in conversation.
Look it up, then keep exploring.

s024
00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:29.270
Defeat monsters
by recalling words you’ve learned!

s025
00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:33.690
With spaced repetition, words come back
at carefully timed intervals,

s026
00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:36.190
helping you build lasting vocabulary.

s027
00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.300
Learn and practice essential grammar rules
through mini-games.

s028
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:44.940
Keep practicing through memory games,
word searches, deduction puzzles,

s029
00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.100
conjugation battleship,
and many more mini-games!

s030
00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.750
Immerse yourself in your target language
with a deeper story.

s031
00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:57.550
Every quest, every battle, and every mystery
brings you closer to fluency.

s032
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.230
WonderLang Beyond introduces
knowledge-based progression.

s033
00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:07.180
Explore different regions freely,
listen carefully to conversations,

s034
00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.500
and search for clues.

s034b
00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.590
Connect what you learn across the world

s035
00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:13.030
to solve mysteries
and unlock new paths.

s036
00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:17.800
Several regions open early,
so you can follow several leads.

s037
00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.150
Your knowledge drives the adventure.

s038
00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.960
The first languages to be released will be

s038b
00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:25.850
French, German,

s039
00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.820
Japanese, Mandarin Chinese, English,

s040
00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.140
Latin American Spanish, and Korean.

s041
00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.650
Help us bring WonderLang Beyond to life!

s042
00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:38.700
With your support, we can create
a bigger, richer learning experience.

s043
00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.730
Back the campaign today and join us

s044
00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.570
in making a true language-learning adventure
once more.

s045
00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:55.810
[Voices in several languages]
Take your language skills further.

s046
00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.300
Take your language skills Beyond.
